{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Approaching deadlines can indeed be a source of stress, which may exacerbate acid reflux symptoms. Stress and anxiety can increase the production of stomach acid and encourage behaviors such as eating quickly or consuming trigger foods, both of which can worsen reflux.  Over-the-counter (OTC) medications can help manage acid reflux. Antacids, like Tums or Maalox, can neutralize stomach acid and provide quick relief. H2 blockers, such as Pepcid or Zantac, reduce the amount of acid your stomach produces and can provide longer-lasting relief. Proton pump inhibitors (PPIs) like Prilosec OTC or Nexium 24HR are more effective for frequent heartburn as they block acid production more effectively and allow time for damaged esophageal tissue to heal. However, it's essential to use these medications according to the directions and consult a healthcare professional if you rely on them frequently or your symptoms persist. Adjusting your lifestyle, such as incorporating stress-reducing techniques, eating smaller meals, and avoiding late-night eating, can be beneficial along with medication.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0030-64-11346:13": 8.293144226074219, "clueweb22-en0004-92-06401:8": 7.80927038192749, "clueweb22-en0002-87-15707:6": 7.645639419555664, "clueweb22-en0046-28-07406:2": 7.562880992889404, "clueweb22-en0030-73-19245:0": 7.503447532653809, "clueweb22-en0004-92-06401:9": 7.421038627624512, "clueweb22-en0002-87-15707:7": 7.327576160430908, "clueweb22-en0010-02-10612:14": 7.246645450592041, "clueweb22-en0006-71-01643:18": 7.2379608154296875, "clueweb22-en0046-28-07406:3": 7.193047046661377}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I want to stop doom scrolling.", "I have gained weight recently because I stopped exercising for the last 6 months.", "I spend too much time on my phone.", "I want to change my lifestyle."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0030-