{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "2-1_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Liberica and Excelsa beans both have unique characteristics, including their caffeine content and appearance.   Liberica beans are typically larger and have an unusual, asymmetrical shape, often described as resembling irregular shells. They usually contain less caffeine compared to Robustas but can vary depending on the specific variety and growing conditions. The beans produce a bold, smoky flavor profile that some might find acquired, while others enjoy its distinctive taste.  Excelsa beans, recently categorized as part of the Liberica family, are similarly large, but they maintain a more uniform, teardrop shape. In terms of caffeine, Excelsa beans fall between Arabica and Robusta, offering moderate caffeine levels. They provide a unique flavor profile with tart, fruity notes and a bright acidity that adds complexity to coffee blends. Their distinct taste and growing appeal suggest that the popularity of Excelsa beans may increase in the future.  Both types of beans offer unique flavors and experiences, providing interesting options for coffee enthusiasts seeking something different from the more common Arabica and Robusta varieties.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0013-48-02026:10": 15.0664701461792, "clueweb22-en0024-80-13694:2": 14.821131706237793, "clueweb22-en0029-40-16358:6": 14.722847938537598, "clueweb22-en0028-32-12803:10": 14.684253692626953, "clueweb22-en0013-59-03217:2": 14.534119606018066, "clueweb22-en0006-47-01686:2": 14.378077507019043, "clueweb22-en0016-86-00585:1": 14.284518241882324, "clueweb22-en0005-30-03345:16": 14.249737739562988, "clueweb22-en0039-84-11607:3": 14.129240989685059, "clueweb22-en0003-00-04486:10": 14.103401184082031}, "ptkb_provenance": ["Excelsa has recently been reclassified as a type of Liberica coffee because it thrives in the same conditions and grows a similarly tall tree. But the actual coffee it produces is vastly different. It has a much fruitier character than Liberica, with a tart acidity that makes it popular for adding complexity to coffee blends. Excelsa coffee makes up only about 7% of the current coffee market. Still, given its appealing flavor profile and the fact that it is nearly as resilient and productive as Robusta, this seems likely to grow. Much like Robusta, Excelsa coffee has been regarded as poor quality, but this is more due to poor growing and processing practices than the bean itself. With the proper care, Excelsa has the potential to be specialty-grade coffee.", "Liberica beans make up only about 2% of the world's current coffee crop. Once upon a time, this varietal was far more critical after disease wiped out much of the world's Arabica supply. Arabica has since made a comeback, and Liberica production has primarily ceased. However, that may change in the future, as climate change makes it increasingly challenging to produce the more sensitive Arabica plants reliably. Liberica coffee has a unique flavor, pairing floral and fruity notes with a deep smokiness that some describe as woody. It has a full-bodied, reminiscent of Robusta coffee. It's not to everyone's taste, but there are some exceptional Liberica coffees to be had when done right."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0013-48-02026:10": 15.0664701461792, "clueweb22-en0024-80-13694:2": 14.821131706237793, "clueweb22-en0029-40-16358:6": 14.722847938537598, "clueweb22-en0028-32-12803:10": 14.684253692626953, "clueweb22-en0013-59-03217:2": 14.534119606018066, "clueweb22-en0006-47-01686:2": 14.378077507019043, "clueweb22-en0016-86-00585:1": 14.284518241882324, "clueweb22-en0005-30-03345:16": 14.249737739562988, "clueweb22-en0039-84-11607:3": 14.129240989685059, "clueweb22-en0003-00-04486:10": 14.103401184082031, "clueweb22-en0026-91-15281:8": 14.022658348083496, "clueweb22-en0021-99-05986:6": 14.011820793151855, "clueweb22-en0026-82-04612:3": 14.01153564453125, "clueweb22