{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "2-1_11", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Roasting significantly impacts coffee beans' flavor, aroma, and acidity. During roasting, chemical reactions occur that transform the beans\u2019 intrinsic qualities. Light roasts, also known as \u201ccinnamon roast,\u201d retain most of the beans' original characteristics like distinct origin flavors and higher acidity. They often have a fruity or floral profile and retain more caffeine than darker roasts. Medium roasts, sometimes referred to as \u201ccity roast,\u201d strike a balance by developing sweeter, fuller flavors without entirely sacrificing the beans' natural characteristics. They have a balanced acidity and aroma, with a slight increase in body. Dark roasts, such as \u201cFrench\u201d or \u201cItalian\u201d roasts, are roasted until the beans develop a deep-bodied flavor, often resulting in chocolatey, nutty, or even smoky notes. These roasts tend to have lower acidity due to the caramelization and Maillard reaction during roasting, offering a smooth and rich taste. However, they can overshadow the bean's natural flavors, resulting in a more homogeneous profile across various beans. Moreover, while the bold taste of dark roasts might suggest higher caffeine content, they actually contain slightly less caffeine than their lighter counterparts.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0036-21-16351:4": 15.79039478302002, "clueweb22-en0011-55-07210:14": 14.639799118041992, "clueweb22-en0043-72-19569:4": 14.590347290039062, "clueweb22-en0035-28-17781:10": 14.53683090209961, "clueweb22-en0019-88-13848:5": 14.40815544128418, "clueweb22-en0031-16-17635:9": 14.353374481201172, "clueweb22-en0036-21-16351:3": 14.1547269821167, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:13": 14.104181289672852, "clueweb22-en0003-90-16104:2": 14.029834747314453, "clueweb22-en0043-72-19569:5": 13.83664608001709}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I occasionally experience mild acid refl