{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-1_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "If you choose not to rest, especially with a suspected pulley injury, you risk worsening the condition. Continuing to climb or perform activities that stress the injured area can lead to a complete rupture of the A2 pulley, which may result in bowstringing. This occurs when the tendon lifts off the bone, making it difficult to fully utilize your finger's strength and dexterity. Over time, this can cause chronic pain and alter your finger's function, impacting your ability to climb or perform daily tasks effectively. Poorly healed injuries can also result in long-term stiffness, reduced grip strength, and increased susceptibility to future injuries. It's important to prioritize rest and rehabilitation to ensure your finger heals properly, allowing you to return to climbing at your best level. Consulting with a healthcare provider experienced in climbing injuries can help you develop a recovery plan tailored to your situation, even without an MRI.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:7": 10.834007263183594, "clueweb22-en0000-18-09663:4": 9.343957901000977, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:8": 8.80438232421875, "clueweb22-en0000-18-09663:3": 8.64781665802002, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:2": 8.192301750183105, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:7": 6.595890998840332, "clueweb22-en0000-18-09663:2": 6.56791353225708, "clueweb22-en0021-61-12131:10": 6.4170403480529785, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:9": 6.311762809753418, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:6": 6.225490093231201}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am climbing regularly for the past 3 years.", "I climb outdoors.", "Many years ago I had a bad fall while bouldering."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:7": 10.834007263183594, "clueweb22-en0000-18-09663:4": 9.343957901000977, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:8": 8.80438232421875, "clueweb22-en0000-18-09663:3": 8.64781665802002, "clueweb22-en0007-15-0979