{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To tape your finger effectively and support injured pulleys, especially the A2 and A3, consider using the H-taping method, which has been shown to keep tendons close to the bone and support the pulleys under pressure. Here\u2019s a step-by-step guide:  1. **Prepare the Tape**: Use a rigid athletic tape, preferably 10cm long and 1.5cm wide. The Leukoplast brand is recommended.  2. **Cut the Tape**: Cut the tape in half lengthwise from both ends, leaving a bridge of about 1cm in the middle, forming an \"H\" shape.  3. **Position**: With your finger straight, place the tape on the injured finger. The bridge should sit on the inside crease of the joint on the upper end of the injured pulley.  4. **Wrap the Tape**: Flex your finger to about 60\u00b0 at the joint. Wrap the upper strip around your finger in a ring, then wrap the lower strip below the joint.  5. **Retape Regularly**: Tape stretches quickly, so retape between each route to maintain effectiveness.  This technique is intended to limit movement at the joint and reduce strain on the injured pulley.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:10": 8.053486824035645, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 7.682977199554443, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:8": 7.460090160369873, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:9": 7.453883647918701, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 7.248134136199951, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:2": 7.244884967803955, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:1": 7.18564510345459, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:6": 7.127503395080566, "clueweb22-en0017-96-08323:5": 7.12741756439209, "clueweb22-en0012-60-11476:18": 7.076830863952637}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am climbing regularly for the past 3 years.", "I climb outdoors."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:10": 8.053486824035645, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 7.682977199554443, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:8": 7.460090160369873, "clueweb22-en0