{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "H-taping is highly effective for supporting injured finger pulleys by keeping tendons close to the bone and reducing stress during activities like crimping. To apply H-taping, follow these steps:   1. Cut a piece of rigid athletic tape about 10 cm long and 1.5 cm wide.  2. Cut the tape in half lengthwise from both ends, leaving a 1 cm bridge in the middle. 3. Slightly flex your finger (around 60\u00b0) and place the tape on the injured finger, ensuring the bridge sits on the palmar side of the joint, aligning with the crease of the upper end of the injured pulley. 4. Wrap one end of the tape over the top of the finger, securing it in a ring above the joint.  5. Secure the other end of the tape below the joint in a similar manner.  H-taping provides significant support while allowing some movement, and research even suggests it can increase crimping strength by an average of 13%. It's a great way to protect your finger as you continue with your climbing activities.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 11.613367080688477, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 10.997405052185059, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:9": 9.993693351745605, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:8": 9.781755447387695, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:9": 9.249408721923828, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:6": 9.08346939086914, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:5": 8.824821472167969, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:14": 8.816376686096191, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:8": 8.737080574035645, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:4": 8.72930908203125}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 11.613367080688477, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 10.997405052185059, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:9": 9.993693351745605, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:8": 9.781755447387695, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:9": 9.249408721923828, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:6": 9.08346939086914, "clueweb22-en0033-8