{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-1_11", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Taking a two-week vacation in January can be a great break, and it's still early enough before your race in April to not disrupt your training significantly. During your vacation, aim to maintain some level of activity, but give yourself the freedom to enjoy your time away. You could incorporate light runs or walks to keep your fitness on track if time and location allow. If you visit places like beaches or parks, consider doing some bodyweight exercises or short runs. Swimming or cycling are also excellent low-impact alternatives if available.   When you return from the vacation, quickly assess your fitness level. You may want to repeat the last couple of weeks of your training plan to build back any lost endurance and keep on track. This approach will help you transition smoothly back into your routine without overwhelming yourself. Remember, consistency is more important than intensity, especially this far in advance. Enjoy your vacation and the change of pace it brings, knowing that you'll return ready to continue your preparation.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-80-15988:11": 10.996076583862305, "clueweb22-en0027-28-02024:16": 9.802985191345215, "clueweb22-en0033-80-15988:10": 9.514065742492676, "clueweb22-en0010-05-19461:1": 9.37679386138916, "clueweb22-en0021-15-15237:1": 9.294617652893066, "clueweb22-en0010-05-19461:2": 9.064330101013184, "clueweb22-en0021-15-15237:0": 8.922445297241211, "clueweb22-en0010-05-19461:3": 8.867963790893555, "clueweb22-en0014-74-08931:4": 8.84718132019043, "clueweb22-en0010-05-19461:0": 8.839420318603516}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am not very confident in my fitness level.", "I live in Spain."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0033-80-15988:11": 10.996076583862305, "clueweb22-en0027-28-02024:16": 9.802985191345215, "clueweb22-en0033-80-15988:10": 9.514065742492676, "clueweb22-en0010-05-19461:1":