{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "While orange juice does have health benefits such as being a good source of vitamin C, it is also high in natural sugars and lacks the fiber found in whole fruit, which can lead to quicker spikes in blood sugar if consumed in large amounts. For healthier alternatives to sugar, you can consider several options:  1. **Stevia:** This natural sweetener is extracted from the leaves of the stevia plant and is calorie-free. It doesn\u2019t affect blood sugar levels, making it a popular choice for people watching their carb intake.  2. **Xylitol and Erythritol:** These are sugar alcohols used as sweeteners that provide fewer calories than sugar. They have a minimal impact on blood sugar and won't cause the same spikes as regular sugar.  3. **Yacon Syrup:** Made from the root of the yacon plant, this syrup is rich in prebiotics, which can aid digestion. Although it contains natural sugars, it has a lower glycemic index.  4. **Natural Sweeteners (Honey, Molasses, Maple Syrup):** These should be used in moderation as they still contain sugar, but they come with additional nutrients and a richer flavor profile.  All these options can be used to sweeten foods while providing potential health benefits compared to regular sugar.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0013-96-08808:5": 9.856081008911133, "clueweb22-en0026-20-07353:7": 9.68167781829834, "clueweb22-en0037-11-01440:2": 9.493775367736816, "clueweb22-en0040-54-09684:8": 9.331596374511719, "clueweb22-en0011-89-08296:6": 9.249951362609863, "clueweb22-en0014-47-13902:4": 9.174232482910156, "clueweb22-en0007-49-16092:12": 9.167612075805664, "clueweb22-en0034-74-05303:9": 9.139352798461914, "clueweb22-en0018-16-07572:15": 9.137227058410645, "clueweb22-en0007-49-16092:1": 9.125992774963379}, "ptkb_provenance": ["Sometimes I drink fresh orange juice in the afternoon."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en