{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Breastfeeding is generally regarded as a beneficial practice for both the mother and the baby, despite some controversies. It offers several advantages, such as promoting brain development in the baby due to the fatty acids present in breast milk. Additionally, breast milk is easier for the baby to digest compared to formula milk and is available whenever the mother is, which can be quite convenient. It also naturally comes at the right temperature, eliminating the need for heating.  For mothers who are worried about nutrients, breast milk contains the right proportion of carbohydrates, protein, calcium, and fat necessary for a baby\u2019s growth, which might be reassuring considering your concern about calcium intake. Moreover, breastfeeding doesn't require food equipment and is cost-effective compared to formula milk.   It also fosters an emotional bond between the mother and the baby, which can be a profound benefit. If returning to work is a concern, breast milk can be expressed so that others can feed the baby. Overall, breastfeeding can be a positive and fulfilling experience if it aligns with your lifestyle and personal preferences.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0037-36-09941:1": 11.517983436584473, "clueweb22-en0003-75-14598:2": 10.897282600402832, "clueweb22-en0011-87-07940:2": 10.638664245605469, "clueweb22-en0017-54-18029:0": 10.616671562194824, "clueweb22-en0040-26-12629:0": 10.497063636779785, "clueweb22-en0041-17-03856:13": 10.484146118164062, "clueweb22-en0017-40-01483:12": 10.473678588867188, "clueweb22-en0016-99-06528:1": 10.455329895019531, "clueweb22-en0012-99-09332:4": 10.43702507019043, "clueweb22-en0044-81-00967:12": 10.321258544921875}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am a woman."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0037-36-09941:1": 11.517983436584473, "clueweb22-en0003-75-14598:2": 10.897282600402832, "clueweb22-en0011-