{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "When it comes to breastfeeding, it's vital for both the mother's and the baby's health. Breast milk provides the optimal nutrition for infants, with a perfect mix of vitamins, protein, and fat that's easy for them to digest. It also contains antibodies that help the baby fight off viruses and bacteria, reducing the risk of many illnesses. For mothers, breastfeeding supports bonding with the baby and can lower the risk of certain health problems like breast and ovarian cancer. It's generally recommended to breastfeed exclusively for the first six months, then continue breastfeeding along with introducing solid foods until at least the age of one or two. While there may be personal and social considerations, from a health perspective, breastfeeding is beneficial and safe.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0024-11-02217:5": 9.982902526855469, "clueweb22-en0027-63-13036:13": 9.766831398010254, "clueweb22-en0008-26-06180:3": 9.452972412109375, "clueweb22-en0000-76-01068:14": 9.169922828674316, "clueweb22-en0041-39-05257:11": 9.159675598144531, "clueweb22-en0000-76-01068:13": 8.993162155151367, "clueweb22-en0027-63-13036:12": 8.847894668579102, "clueweb22-en0045-30-07949:16": 8.79575252532959, "clueweb22-en0027-52-07425:1": 8.657487869262695, "clueweb22-en0002-06-12527:6": 8.623941421508789}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I think I don't get enough calcium, and I am worried about it.", "I am a woman."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0024-11-02217:5": 9.982902526855469, "clueweb22-en0027-63-13036:13": 9.766831398010254, "clueweb22-en0008-26-06180:3": 9.452972412109375, "clueweb22-en0000-76-01068:14": 9.169922828674316, "clueweb22-en0041-39-05257:11": 9.159675598144531, "clueweb22-en0000-76-01068:13": 8.993162155151367, "clueweb22-en0027-63-13036:12": 8.847894668579102, "clueweb22-en0045-30-07949:16": 8.79575252532959, "clueweb22-en0027-52-07425:1": 8.