{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "While it's natural to hope your baby won't cry often, it's important to understand that crying is a normal and healthy way for newborns to communicate their needs. Babies usually cry for specific reasons like hunger, discomfort due to dirty diapers, being too hot or cold, or needing to be burped after feeding. Newborns also cry when they're tired or in an uncomfortable position. Some crying is inevitable as your baby expresses their needs, but by understanding these signals, you'll be more equipped to respond to them effectively.  Taking steps like maintaining a regular feeding schedule, ensuring your baby is comfortable and dressed appropriately, and keeping them clean and dry can help minimize crying. Also, if your baby seems gassy or bloated, try burping them after feeds to provide relief. Remember, crying is a natural part of your baby's development and helps you bond as you learn to meet their needs. It's perfectly normal for newborns to cry, and over time, you'll become more adept at understanding and soothing your baby.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0022-95-15389:7": 7.5185546875, "clueweb22-en0035-37-13460:2": 7.424600601196289, "clueweb22-en0013-14-15472:6": 7.276296138763428, "clueweb22-en0037-12-05432:17": 7.215445041656494, "clueweb22-en0017-08-10021:1": 7.095656871795654, "clueweb22-en0030-55-13456:15": 7.011492729187012, "clueweb22-en0001-45-04808:12": 6.990688800811768, "clueweb22-en0000-31-08876:17": 6.911021709442139, "clueweb22-en0023-90-07645:1": 6.91091775894165, "clueweb22-en0017-08-10021:4": 6.855507850646973}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am a woman."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0022-95-15389:7": 7.5185546875, "clueweb22-en0035-37-13460:2": 7.424600601196289, "clueweb22-en0013-14-15472:6": 7.276296138763428, "clueweb22-en0037-12-05432:17": 7.215445041656494, "clueweb22-en0017-08-10021:1": 7.095656871795654, "c