{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The main difference between fractional and fully ablative CO2 laser treatments lies in how they interact with the skin. Fractional CO2 lasers target only a fraction of the skin in a pixelated pattern, leaving surrounding areas untouched. This targeted approach helps to promote faster healing and reduces side effects when compared to fully ablative treatments. Fractional treatments are effective for mild to moderate signs of aging, uneven texture, and hyperpigmentation, making the skin appear smoother and more uniform in color.  On the other hand, fully ablative CO2 lasers remove the entire top layer of the skin in the treated area, allowing new skin to regenerate. This method can produce more dramatic results in terms of wrinkle and scar reduction. However, it involves a more intense procedure that typically requires general anesthesia, with a longer recovery period of at least two weeks, during which the skin can be red, swollen, and scabbed.  For someone looking for noticeable improvements with minimal downtime, as in your case, fractional treatments might offer a more suitable blend of effectiveness and recovery time.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:9": 10.041006088256836, "clueweb22-en0016-51-15456:6": 9.127246856689453, "clueweb22-en0022-44-12230:2": 9.10515022277832, "clueweb22-en0009-27-04860:7": 9.082552909851074, "clueweb22-en0014-86-08050:7": 9.05777645111084, "clueweb22-en0009-27-04860:6": 8.982403755187988, "clueweb22-en0031-16-03068:4": 8.920259475708008, "clueweb22-en0022-56-04360:2": 8.872614860534668, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:10": 8.862874031066895, "clueweb22-en0009-27-04860:5": 8.737984657287598}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I've noticed dark spots and uneven tone on my face.", "I have visible pores on my cheeks and nose.", "I usually wear makeup to even out my complexion.", "I'm interested in treatments th