{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_11", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Yes, you can generally continue with your skincare routine after microneedling, but it's important to make some adjustments to ensure optimal healing and results. Immediately after the treatment, your skin may be more sensitive, so you'll want to avoid using any harsh products, particularly those that contain active ingredients like retinol or vitamin C, during the first few days post-procedure. These could potentially cause irritation on your healing skin.  For the initial healing period, focus on using gentle, hydrating products to soothe and nourish your skin. Your usual hyaluronic acid is a good choice, as it helps to maintain moisture and support skin repair. Make sure to apply a broad-spectrum, non-comedogenic sunscreen daily to protect your skin from UV damage, as it will be more susceptible to sun exposure after microneedling.  Once your skin has had a chance to recover, typically after about a week, you can gradually reintroduce your regular products like vitamin C and retinol, one at a time, monitoring for any signs of sensitivity. As always, it's a good idea to consult with your dermatologist or skincare professional for personalized advice tailored to your specific skin needs and concerns.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0026-93-18119:7": 13.114888191223145, "clueweb22-en0036-10-01168:9": 12.877714157104492, "clueweb22-en0016-80-15701:8": 12.784515380859375, "clueweb22-en0030-29-13584:9": 12.740631103515625, "clueweb22-en0030-73-16433:9": 12.654293060302734, "clueweb22-en0040-82-05127:9": 12.622647285461426, "clueweb22-en0033-92-13251:4": 12.583806037902832, "clueweb22-en0030-73-16433:12": 12.542458534240723, "clueweb22-en0036-10-01168:8": 12.521110534667969, "clueweb22-en0000-24-11991:12": 12.445707321166992}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I use vitamin C and Retinol every day in my morning routine.", "I usually wear makeup to e