{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-2_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "For managing both an oily scalp and dry hair, it's essential to find a balanced shampoo that addresses each issue. Look for a shampoo that is lightweight but effectively cleanses the scalp while providing hydration to the hair strands. Opt for a gentle clarifying shampoo with salicylic acid or tea tree oil to help control excess oil on the scalp without over-stripping moisture from your hair. Additionally, ingredients like niacinamide and lactic acid can help balance the scalp's oil production.  To maintain moisture in your dry hair, follow up with a lightweight, hydrating conditioner focusing on the mid-lengths and ends. Avoid applying conditioner near the scalp to prevent added greasiness. Make sure to reduce the use of heat styling tools or use a heat protectant when styling to prevent further dryness. Regularly clean your hairbrushes and pillowcases to reduce the transfer of oil and bacteria. Balancing your hair care routine and being mindful of product placement will help manage both conditions effectively.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0010-84-04941:8": 15.28260326385498, "clueweb22-en0012-95-06097:1": 14.833452224731445, "clueweb22-en0021-86-00233:14": 14.779194831848145, "clueweb22-en0044-75-14432:4": 14.589293479919434, "clueweb22-en0012-95-06097:0": 14.482680320739746, "clueweb22-en0038-13-14402:2": 14.449409484863281, "clueweb22-en0025-40-13157:5": 14.373351097106934, "clueweb22-en0010-84-04941:9": 14.308540344238281, "clueweb22-en0041-54-13093:6": 14.261540412902832, "clueweb22-en0044-95-03460:11": 14.242574691772461}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I frequently use heat styling tools to keep my hair looking good."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0010-84-04941:8": 15.28260326385498, "clueweb22-en0012-95-06097:1": 14.833452224731445, "clueweb22-en0021-86-00233:14": 14.779194831848145, "clueweb22-en0044-75-14432:4": 14.589293479919