{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "7-1_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Great! Here are a couple of healthy bread recipes you might enjoy trying at home:  1. **Whole Wheat Bread**: Start with 3 cups of whole wheat flour, 1 packet of active dry yeast, 1 to 1 1/4 cups of warm water, 2 tablespoons of honey, 1 tablespoon of olive oil, and a pinch of salt. Mix the yeast with warm water and let it sit until foamy. Add the honey and oil, then gradually incorporate the flour and salt. Knead until smooth, let it rise until doubled, shape into a loaf, and bake at 180\u00b0C (350\u00b0F) for about 30 minutes.  2. **Seeded Oat Bread**: Mix 2 cups of whole grain oats, 1 cup of mixed seeds (like sunflower, flax, and chia), 1/4 cup of whole wheat flour, 1 teaspoon of salt, and 1 teaspoon of baking soda. Combine with 1 3/4 cups of buttermilk and 1 tablespoon of honey. Pour into a lined loaf pan and bake at 180\u00b0C (350\u00b0F) for 50-60 minutes.  Both recipes incorporate nutritious ingredients and are perfect for sharing with family or guests. Enjoy the challenge and the delightful taste of homemade bread!", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0021-77-14804:5": 12.406217575073242, "clueweb22-en0037-18-14951:6": 11.934248924255371, "clueweb22-en0006-47-03568:5": 11.934014320373535, "clueweb22-en0038-91-04137:14": 11.902923583984375, "clueweb22-en0002-62-15463:4": 11.707476615905762, "clueweb22-en0010-89-18695:4": 11.705316543579102, "clueweb22-en0039-63-13992:11": 11.701974868774414, "clueweb22-en0035-16-00216:4": 11.685748100280762, "clueweb22-en0035-16-00216:3": 11.640922546386719, "clueweb22-en0002-99-03493:1": 11.614757537841797}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I often eat raw salads.", "I enjoy baking.", "I avoid frying food at home due to the smell."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0021-77-14804:5": 12.406217575073242, "clueweb22-en0037-18-14951:6": 11.934248924255371, "clueweb22-en0006-47-03568:5": 11.934014320373535, "clueweb