{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "7-1_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Turkish bread and lavash are both delicious options, but they have distinct characteristics. Turkish bread is known for its soft and airy texture with a slightly chewy crust, making it ideal as a complementary bread for soups, salads, or as a sandwich base. It often features a simple white flour base, sometimes enriched with yogurt for additional softness. Turkish flatbreads can also be versatile, used for wraps or simply enjoyed with olive oil and herbs.  Lavash, on the other hand, is a thin flatbread, often low in calories, and traditionally made using a basic mixture of flour, water, and salt. Its thinness makes it more pliable when fresh, suitable for rolling and wrapping, making it a great base for rolled sandwiches or wraps. Lavash can also be baked until crispy, turning it into a cracker-like bread, perfect for dipping.  Both breads can complement healthy diets and are particularly good with fresh salads or foods you've smoked at home, with lavash providing a lighter and simpler base while Turkish bread offers a more substantial and chewy option. Enjoy experimenting with both to see which suits your culinary creations best!", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0041-64-01489:3": 13.84985065460205, "clueweb22-en0041-64-01489:2": 13.467455863952637, "clueweb22-en0044-75-13848:4": 13.17335319519043, "clueweb22-en0044-75-13848:5": 12.778179168701172, "clueweb22-en0044-75-13848:3": 12.77426815032959, "clueweb22-en0012-75-15335:7": 12.319826126098633, "clueweb22-en0012-75-15335:2": 12.3176908493042, "clueweb22-en0023-44-17198:11": 12.269918441772461, "clueweb22-en0040-10-10299:12": 12.159833908081055, "clueweb22-en0012-75-15335:15": 12.141457557678223}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I often eat raw salads.", "I like to share food with guests or family."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0041-64-01489:3": 13.84985065460205, "clueweb22-en0041-64-01489