{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_4", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "It sounds like managing multiple tasks is a challenge due to difficulty maintaining focus. Here are a few strategies that might help:  1. **Prioritize Tasks**: Choose two priority tasks for the day. Switch between them when your attention starts fading, but avoid jumping to tasks beyond these two. This can reduce the cycle of starting many tasks without completion.  2. **Pomodoro Technique**: Use this time-management method to work in focused intervals. Set a timer for 25 minutes to work on one task, then take a short break. This can help maintain focus and make tasks feel more manageable.  3. **Use Movement for Focus**: While seated, consider using tools like a balance ball chair or a fidget spinner. These can provide subtle movement, which might help maintain your concentration given your sedentary lifestyle.  4. **Structured Routine**: Develop a daily routine to add structure. A routine can help maintain focus and manage energy levels throughout the day.  Feel free to experiment with these approaches and see which ones best fit your needs.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0042-03-14870:5": 9.804807662963867, "clueweb22-en0041-10-01075:17": 9.783916473388672, "clueweb22-en0030-53-01118:15": 9.671163558959961, "clueweb22-en0036-69-02673:4": 9.337491989135742, "clueweb22-en0045-61-12916:14": 9.166055679321289, "clueweb22-en0042-03-14870:7": 9.107816696166992, "clueweb22-en0038-46-17021:18": 8.873099327087402, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:4": 8.680432319641113, "clueweb22-en0040-96-06329:3": 8.67629337310791, "clueweb22-en0036-02-14625:3": 8.650774002075195}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I work in an office.", "I live in Germany."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0042-03-14870:5": 9.804807662963867, "clueweb22-en0041-10-01075:17": 9.783916473388672, "clueweb22-en0030-53-01118:15": 9.671163558959961, "clueweb22-en0036-69-02673:4": 9.33749198913574