{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To manage ADHD symptoms by alternating between tasks, you can use the Pomodoro Technique or a similar time management tool. Here's how it typically works: Set a timer for a short, focused work session\u2014usually 25 minutes\u2014dedicated to one task. This limited time commitment makes it easier to concentrate. After the timer goes off, take a short break of about 5 minutes. During this break, step away from your work to recharge and clear your mind. After the break, switch to another task, again setting a timer for focused work. This method lets you harness bursts of energy and maintains your interest by providing variety, which is especially helpful for someone who loves daydreaming or storytelling, as these intervals allow mental wandering while still accomplishing tasks. Repeat this cycle throughout the day. Over time, you\u2019ll train your brain to focus and transition smoothly, improving your overall productivity. Since you enjoy quiet settings and can sleep anywhere, use breaks to relax and ensure your workspace remains a haven of calm, increasing effectiveness.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0007-85-19058:7": 11.859041213989258, "clueweb22-en0016-99-04355:1": 11.451752662658691, "clueweb22-en0030-19-05230:2": 11.320035934448242, "clueweb22-en0007-85-19058:8": 10.64478874206543, "clueweb22-en0041-06-04526:2": 10.540266990661621, "clueweb22-en0007-85-19058:4": 10.33084487915039, "clueweb22-en0007-85-19058:14": 10.161200523376465, "clueweb22-en0030-19-05230:8": 10.145071983337402, "clueweb22-en0007-85-19058:15": 10.077370643615723, "clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:8": 9.916948318481445}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0007-85-19058:7": 11.859041213989258, "clueweb22-en0016-99-04355:1": 11.451752662658691, "clueweb22-en0030-19-05230:2": 11.320035934448242, "clueweb22-en0007-85-19058:8": 10.64478874206543, "clue