{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "If you find the Pomodoro Technique too strict or don't like interrupting your hyperfocus, consider incorporating a more flexible approach. Instead of using a timer, try to recognize your natural focus cycles. When you're in a state of hyperfocus, allow yourself to maintain that momentum until you feel a natural lull. Once you notice your concentration starting to wane, use this as a cue to take a brief, meaningful break. Given your love for quiet and enjoyment of cooking, stepping away from your desk to prepare a quick snack or doing some light stretching might help recharge your mind.  Another strategy you might find helpful is setting broad but achievable goals for the day. Focus on completing a few key tasks without rigid time constraints. This approach allows the flexibility to adapt your strategy based on how you feel throughout the day.  Finally, build these practices into a schedule that accommodates both focused work and the inevitable distractions. Balancing productivity with your natural rhythm can make your workday feel more seamless and less regimented.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0004-59-16742:12": 17.22903060913086, "clueweb22-en0001-49-04668:16": 16.823020935058594, "clueweb22-en0012-51-00120:11": 16.77945327758789, "clueweb22-en0027-34-14560:2": 16.674623489379883, "clueweb22-en0012-51-00120:12": 16.652475357055664, "clueweb22-en0003-44-15078:12": 16.522987365722656, "clueweb22-en0015-94-05578:0": 16.501590728759766, "clueweb22-en0012-91-02398:18": 16.239160537719727, "clueweb22-en0033-18-04361:4": 16.186769485473633, "clueweb22-en0041-12-11924:11": 16.079933166503906}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I work in an office.", "I have a sedentary lifestyle."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0004-59-16742:12": 17.22903060913086, "clueweb22-en0001-49-04668:16": 16.823020935058594, "clueweb22-en0012-51-00120:11": 16.77945327758789,