{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To manage distractions during hyperfocus periods effectively, a few strategies can help. First, minimize interruptions by setting your computer and phone to \"do not disturb\" mode, which will prevent notifications from popping up. Consider disabling email alerts and scheduling specific times to check and respond to your emails, rather than allowing them to interrupt your focus. If you have meetings, try to schedule them outside of your peak workflow times. Also, use a distraction-blocking app on your computer to prevent access to non-essential websites.  If an unavoidable distraction happens, like an urgent email or meeting, jot down what you were working on and your next steps before addressing the distraction. This makes it easier to return to your task with a clear plan. To further guard your hyperfocus periods, communicate with colleagues about your needs for undistracted time, especially if your tasks require intense focus. By preparing for potential distractions ahead of time, you can maintain your flow state more effectively.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0014-54-13628:2": 11.485916137695312, "clueweb22-en0022-33-08001:9": 10.904783248901367, "clueweb22-en0034-82-00974:1": 10.833686828613281, "clueweb22-en0007-63-12388:2": 10.828423500061035, "clueweb22-en0006-80-11686:3": 10.81969928741455, "clueweb22-en0022-21-03294:11": 10.662769317626953, "clueweb22-en0041-12-03522:5": 10.62394905090332, "clueweb22-en0016-22-09673:7": 10.617494583129883, "clueweb22-en0014-73-14286:7": 10.599206924438477, "clueweb22-en0014-54-13628:1": 10.579538345336914}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I work in an office.", "I have a sedentary lifestyle.", "I live in Germany."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0014-54-13628:2": 11.485916137695312, "clueweb22-en0022-33-08001:9": 10.904783248901367, "clueweb22-en0034-82-00974:1": 10.833686828613281, "clueweb22-en000