{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To manage meetings that disrupt your hyperfocus, try a few strategies. Before diving into a focused work session, check your schedule for upcoming meetings so you aren't caught off guard. If possible, block out periods of deep focus work on your calendar, signaling to colleagues when you're unavailable for meetings.   In case a meeting interrupts your flow, try to have a quick task or note prepared to smoothly transition back into work afterward. After the meeting, take a moment to jot down key points and actions required, then allow yourself a few minutes to refocus before returning to your task.   If meetings disrupt your day too often, consider discussing with your manager about clustering them into specific times of day to maintain longer focus periods before or after. Additionally, scheduling regular work slots where you're less available for meetings can help you set boundaries and protect your productive time.   These strategies can help balance necessary meetings with your hyperfocus periods, allowing for better flow and task completion.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0045-83-07959:6": 11.832977294921875, "clueweb22-en0022-32-12876:4": 11.379441261291504, "clueweb22-en0007-48-14700:4": 11.376110076904297, "clueweb22-en0022-32-12876:5": 11.3212251663208, "clueweb22-en0012-33-13598:3": 11.008408546447754, "clueweb22-en0030-54-15087:3": 10.884685516357422, "clueweb22-en0036-68-15104:5": 10.80446720123291, "clueweb22-en0014-63-15541:4": 10.723695755004883, "clueweb22-en0041-82-15799:2": 10.705208778381348, "clueweb22-en0026-11-19268:9": 10.692662239074707}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I work in an office.", "I have a sedentary lifestyle."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0045-83-07959:6": 11.832977294921875, "clueweb22-en0022-32-12876:4": 11.379441261291504, "clueweb22-en0007-48-14700:4": 11.376110076904297, "clueweb22-en0022-32-12876:5