{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-1_11", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Clipless pedals could be worth considering for your mountain biking, given your style and the terrains you ride on. They provide a secure connection between your shoes and the pedals, improving pedaling efficiency and power transfer. This is particularly beneficial for long rides or rough trails where maintaining consistent pedal power is important. Although they require a learning curve as you need to kick your heel out to disengage, the ease of clipping in and out of modern systems makes them quite user-friendly. Moreover, as you often navigate hilly and rough paths, the added control they offer can be valuable, especially for downhill or technical sections.   However, since comfort is a priority for you, it's important to choose clipless shoes and pedals that provide good comfort and match your riding habits. Given your occasional overwhelm with technical choices, it might be helpful to consult a local bike shop to find a setup that fits well and matches your needs. If you're unsure, starting with flat pedals and upgrading later could also be an option, helping you transition gradually.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0037-60-07465:5": 15.855767250061035, "clueweb22-en0036-51-05870:7": 15.314790725708008, "clueweb22-en0021-36-08429:13": 15.282196044921875, "clueweb22-en0002-05-13020:5": 15.207390785217285, "clueweb22-en0040-66-10035:1": 14.927070617675781, "clueweb22-en0035-07-03614:2": 14.84695816040039, "clueweb22-en0021-36-08429:12": 14.762307167053223, "clueweb22-en0030-36-02569:2": 14.749528884887695, "clueweb22-en0036-51-05870:13": 14.613443374633789, "clueweb22-en0036-51-05870:2": 14.55379581451416}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am a casual bike rider.", "I recently moved to a city with more hills and rough paths.", "I like biking even in rainy weather and in the forest.", "I value comfort over speed.", "I care about sustainabil