{"metadata": {"team_id": "uva", "run_id": "disco-qrecc", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To determine when to add grease to your bike chain again, pay attention to a few key signs. If you notice your chain starting to make a squeaking or grinding noise, it\u2019s likely time for lubrication. Additionally, if your chain appears dry or shows signs of rust, it\u2019s time to clean and re-lubricate it. Regular maintenance is essential, especially if you ride in wet or dirty conditions, like during rainy weather or in the forest. A good rule of thumb is to reapply lubricant every 100-200 miles of riding, or more frequently if conditions are harsh. Remember to clean and dry the chain thoroughly before applying the lubricant to ensure the grease sticks to the chain effectively and doesn\u2019t trap dirt. Using a bicycle-specific chain lubricant is recommended, as it is designed not to attract dirt, keeping your drivetrain components in good condition and your pedaling smooth and efficient.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0028-54-18048:4": 10.36463451385498, "clueweb22-en0002-63-04266:1": 10.238985061645508, "clueweb22-en0019-16-02034:12": 9.988962173461914, "clueweb22-en0036-18-01049:9": 9.932377815246582, "clueweb22-en0046-59-00018:4": 9.876999855041504, "clueweb22-en0033-39-12876:5": 9.87131118774414, "clueweb22-en0023-43-04773:6": 9.805996894836426, "clueweb22-en0028-74-10465:6": 9.779747009277344, "clueweb22-en0020-44-10600:10": 9.678507804870605, "clueweb22-en0004-96-02954:3": 9.638625144958496}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I like biking even in rainy weather and in the forest."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0028-54-18048:4": 10.36463451385498, "clueweb22-en0002-63-04266:1": 10.238985061645508, "clueweb22-en0019-16-02034:12": 9.988962173461914, "clueweb22-en0036-18-01049:9": 9.932377815246582, "clueweb22-en0046-59-00018:4": 9.876999855041504, "clueweb22-en0033-39-12876:5": 9.87131118774414, "clueweb22-en0023-43-04773:6": 9.805